======================================================================================================================
PART 3 -- ADJUDICATING THE PRIOR RESULTS
======================================================================================================================
  g04h ('the causal boost does NOT regenerate P(k): sigma_8 <= 0.65, deficit 20-2000x'):
    CONFIRMED AS STATED, and CORRECTED IN SCOPE.  Its boost is not nu(g/a0); it is a CAUSAL, SATURATING
    B = min[0.9 (c_* k t/a)^2, nu-1] refilling a 28 eV relic's free-streaming cutoff.  The deficit is a
    statement about that construction.  It is NOT a statement about MOND's effect on linear growth, which
    this script finds has the OPPOSITE SIGN.  Quoting g04h as 'MOND under-produces structure' is wrong.
  rising_a0_baryon_only ('tilt 288-317, amplitude 1e6-1e9 too strong on branch B'):
    CONFIRMED independently here: tilt 175-199, branch B far worse than branch A.
  mi_covariant_pt ('the derived Hubble floor gives sigma_8 = 0.829-0.833, LCDM-degenerate'):
    CONFIRMED independently here: sigma_8 = 0.8112.
  [PASS] P3-a  the three prior results are mutually consistent ONCE THEIR SETUPS ARE DISTINGUISHED, and the net statement is: the MOND boost OVERSHOOTS linear growth unless the framework's own Hubble floor is imposed, in which case it does nothing at all.  There is no configuration that both fixes P(k) and leaves a distinctive signal   (unfloored max sigma_8 = 2.12e+03; floored = 0.8112 (= unboosted 0.8101 to 0.1%))

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT (fbC3)
======================================================================================================================

  BARYON-ONLY, MOND-BOOSTED GROWTH FAILS ON SHAPE FOR ANY AMPLITUDE.  The boost nu = sqrt(1 + a0/g_N) is
  largest where the peculiar gravity is smallest, and the peculiar gravity is smallest on SMALL scales at
  early times, so small scales grow fastest and the spectrum arrives tilted by a factor 175-199 in power
  across k = 0.02-20 h/Mpc.  That is a normalisation-free failure: no choice of the initial baryon amplitude
  fixes it.  The amplitude fails too, and it fails UPWARD: sigma_8 = 25.7-2.12e+03 against 0.811.
  Branch B is worse than branch A by orders (2.12e+03 vs 44.3) because a0(z) propto H makes the boost larger at
  every earlier epoch.

  CORRECTION TO THE PRIOR RECORD.  The repository's "growth deficit under a causal boost" (g04h: sigma_8 <=
  0.648, 20-2000x short) is a result about REFILLING A 28 eV RELIC'S FREE-STREAMING CUTOFF with a causal
  saturating boost.  It is not a result about MOND's linear growth, which errs in the opposite direction.
  Both are reproduced here and both stand -- in their own scopes.

  AND THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN ESCAPE IS A DEAD END EITHER WAY.  With its derived dS-Unruh Hubble floor the boost
  collapses to a few per cent (sigma_8 = 0.8112 vs 0.8101 unboosted): the cosmology becomes LCDM's and the
  distinctive content disappears.  Without the floor, and WITH the cold Omega_dm that the CMB requires, the
  boost double-counts and gives sigma_8 = 13.8.  There is no setting that is simultaneously right at the CMB,
  right at sigma_8, and distinctive.

